							<span id="copy-btn-text">Copy Letter</span>
						</button>
						<a class="btn btn--email" id="mailto-btn" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
							<svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect width="20" height="16" x="2" y="4" rx="2"/><path d="m22 7-8.97 5.7a1.94 1.94 0 0 1-2.06 0L2 7"/></svg>
							<span>Open in Email</span>
						</a>
						<button type="button" class="btn btn--print" id="print-btn">
							<svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 6 2 18 2 18 9"/><path d="M6 18H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h16a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-2"/><rect x="6" y="14" width="12" height="8"/></svg>
							<span>Print / PDF</span>
						</button>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Email Preview Sheet -->
				<div class="email-sheet" id="email-sheet">
					<div class="email-sheet__header">
						<div class="email-field"><span class="email-label">To:</span> <span id="preview-to">[support@company.com]</span></div>
						<div class="email-field"><span class="email-label">From:</span> <span id="preview-from">[Your Email Address]</span></div>
						<div class="email-field"><span class="email-label">Subject:</span> <strong id="preview-subject">Subscription Cancellation Request</strong></div>
					</div>
					<div class="email-sheet__body" id="preview-body">
						<!-- Dynamically generated -->
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- CTA Callout -->
				<div class="cta-callout">
					<h3>Tired of chasing hidden cancel buttons one by one?</h3>
					<p>CancelKits scans your inbox in 30 seconds (read-only) to find every recurring subscription and helps you cancel them in one click.</p>
					<a href="/start/" class="cta-callout__btn">Run Free 30-Second Subscription Audit →</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Toast -->
		<div class="toast" id="toast" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copied to clipboard!</div>

		<!-- SEO Educational Content Section -->
		<section class="seo-content">
			<div class="seo-content__inner">
				<h2>How to Guarantee Your Cancellation Request Is Honored</h2>
				<p class="seo-content__intro">
					Companies count on you giving up. Use these four strategies to make sure your cancellation sticks — and get your money back if they keep charging.
				</p>

				<div class="tips-grid">
					<div class="tip-card">
						<div class="tip-num">1</div>
						<h3>Create a Timestamped Paper Trail</h3>
						<p>Always send your cancellation via email (not phone or chat). The email's sent-date timestamp is admissible proof if you need to file a dispute. Take a screenshot of the sent email for your records.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="tip-card">
						<div class="tip-num">2</div>
						<h3>Know Your Chargeback Leverage</h3>
						<p>Under Regulation E (debit) and the Fair Credit Billing Act (credit cards), you have 60 days from the statement date to dispute unauthorized charges. Mention this in your letter — companies know chargebacks cost them $20–75 each in processing fees.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="tip-card">
						<div class="tip-num">3</div>
						<h3>Cite the FTC Click-to-Cancel Rule</h3>
						<p>The FTC's 2024 "Click-to-Cancel" rule (effective 2025) requires companies to offer cancellation methods as easy as sign-up. If a company forces you through a phone call or hidden multi-step process, they may be in violation of federal law.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="tip-card">
						<div class="tip-num">4</div>
						<h3>Use a Virtual Card for Future Trials</h3>
						<p>Services like Privacy.com or your bank's virtual card feature let you create single-use card numbers with spending limits. Even if you forget to cancel a trial, they can't charge a card that no longer works.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- FAQ Section -->
		<section class="clg-faq" id="faq">
			<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<div class="faq-list">
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>Is this cancellation letter generator really free?</summary>
					<p>Yes, 100% free with no login required. The tool runs entirely in your browser — no data is sent to any server, no AI API calls are made, and no personal information is stored. We built it as a free resource for consumers dealing with hard-to-cancel subscriptions.</p>
				</details>
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>Can I use this to get a refund for an auto-renewal I didn't want?</summary>
					<p>Absolutely. Select the "Unwanted Auto-Renewal Refund" or "Forgotten Free Trial Refund" scenario. The generator creates a legally-grounded email citing FTC Click-to-Cancel rules and consumer protection statutes that companies are required to follow. Many companies will issue a refund when presented with a well-written, legally-cited request.</p>
				</details>
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>Does sending a cancellation email legally cancel my subscription?</summary>
					<p>Under the FTC's 2024 Click-to-Cancel rule (effective 2025), companies must provide cancellation methods that are as easy as signing up. A written email creates a timestamped paper trail. If the company ignores it, you have documented proof for a chargeback with your bank or a complaint to the FTC at ReportFraud.ftc.gov.</p>
				</details>
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>What if the company ignores my cancellation email?</summary>
					<p>If the company continues charging you after receiving your cancellation request: (1) File a chargeback/dispute with your bank or credit card issuer — your emailed cancellation serves as evidence. (2) File a complaint with the FTC at ReportFraud.ftc.gov. (3) Report to your state Attorney General's consumer protection division. Most companies settle quickly when faced with chargeback fees and regulatory complaints.</p>
				</details>
				<details class="faq-item">
					<summary>How do I cancel Adobe Creative Cloud without paying the early termination fee?</summary>
					<p>Select "Adobe Creative Cloud" from the service dropdown and choose the "Standard Immediate Cancellation" scenario. The generated letter specifically requests waiving the early termination fee by citing financial hardship or accidental plan selection — Adobe agents have documented authority to waive this fee when customers ask firmly. You can also try Adobe's online chat and reference the FTC Click-to-Cancel rule.</p>
				</details>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>

	<Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   CANCELLATION LETTER GENERATOR — 100% CLIENT-SIDE ENGINE
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

